course: dictionary
lesson: 14211
title: Many cells, one living thing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Look at the word in two parts. Multi- means many, as in multiply, and cell is a tiny building block of living things. So multicellular means made of many cells. «An oak tree is multicellular.» An oak tree is built from millions of cells, and the word itself gives you the clue.
explain: Some living things are made of just one cell. «A bacterium is unicellular.» Uni- means one, so unicellular means made of one cell. Multicellular is the opposite: many cells working together as one living thing.
explain: In a multicellular living thing, different cells do different jobs. «In your body, muscle cells pull and nerve cells carry messages.» When you meet a new word, swap your meaning into the sentence: «A mushroom is made of many cells» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Multicellular means made of many cells.
fact: Multi- means many, and cell means a tiny building block of living things.
fact: Animals, plants and most fungi are multicellular, such as humans, trees and mushrooms.
fact: Unicellular means made of one cell, like bacteria.
exercise: «A dog is multicellular.» What does multicellular mean? | Made of one cell only | Made of stone | Made of water only | *Made of many cells
exercise: Which living thing is unicellular? | A mushroom | *A bacterium | An oak tree | A human
exercise: Look at the word parts. Multi- means many. What does multicellular mean? | Having many legs | Made of many roots | Having many colours | *Made of many cells
test: Which word means made of one cell? | *Unicellular | Multicellular | Multicoloured | Multiplied
test: «In a multicellular animal, nerve cells do an important job.» What is that job? | Make food from sunlight | *Carry messages | Turn into rock | Freeze the body
exam: Which living thing is multicellular? | A single cell | A bacterium | A drop of water | *A mushroom
